1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,800
Elena manages a Bayside franchise, so she needs Harborline’s business application without becoming a Harborline employee.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,400
She starts at the branded Franchise Hub and signs up with her own business email through External ID.

3
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:23,000
A trusted franchise record and location-scoped role decide what the application returns after authentication.

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:31,700
Elena can open the Bayside scorecard and standards, while another owner’s hotel and royalty data remain blocked.

5
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:39,500
The important point is the boundary: External ID establishes the person, and the application enforces company, role and location.
